# Build-context exclusions.
#
# Added with the end-to-end MCP isolation gate (enhancedchannelmanager-04c0u.8),
# which builds the ECM image from a developer checkout rather than only from a
# clean CI clone. Without this, `COPY frontend/ ./` copies a bootstrapped
# worktree's `frontend/node_modules` over the `npm ci` output of the previous
# layer, and a symlinked `.bin` inside it fails the build outright with
# "cannot replace to directory .../node_modules/.bin with file".
#
# Everything listed here is either regenerated inside the image (node_modules,
# dist, virtualenvs) or is not part of the application (VCS metadata, caches,
# test artifacts). Nothing the Dockerfile copies is excluded.
.git
.gitignore
**/node_modules
**/.venv
**/venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
frontend/dist
frontend/coverage
frontend/playwright-report
frontend/test-results
.beads
.vite-temp
